From: jd1100 <248791769+ayooooo123@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 22:04:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(private): Gate D host-path boundary - canonical
 blinded presence records
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Delivers the package-private host-path boundary of blinded presence records
with only vetted primitives, and stops Gate D honestly where the dependency
tree cannot support Tor's full scheme.

Delivered:
- Epoch addressing key k_e = H(domain || A || epoch), keyed BLAKE2b
- Tor v3 [KEYBLIND] A.2 public half: A' = h*A via native constant-time
  crypto_scalarmult_ed25519_noclamp, with Tor's exact clamp; pinned
  byte-exactly against Tor's published test_blinding_basics vector
- Canonical fixed 1023-byte padded records (exit-wire value cap), header
  (version|epoch|zero padding|epoch address) as AEAD associated data
- Owner authentication via stable-identity certificate over the epoch key
  and the exact canonical descriptor digest, carried inside the encrypted
  body; reader credential mandatory, no plaintext mode
- 7-day epochs, 1-day Tor-style overlap window, owner-signed tombstones
  with precedence over descriptors
- 16 brittle tests / 80 assertions registered in the portable aggregate

Blocked, documented in docs/private-routing-migration.md:
- a' = h·a mod L and public verification under the blinded key need a
  constant-time scalar-on-scalar multiply; sodium-universal 5.x does not
  export crypto_core_ed25519_scalar_mul and the only in-tree scalar mul is
  the experimental tweak extension PR47 was reverted for. No JS BigInt
  anywhere; no export; no public required mode; no exit-side presence.

Node aggregate 1034/1034 (19,261 asserts). Bare 18/18 module tests green;
full-suite socket-lifecycle flakes are pre-existing (reproduced on clean
tree) and unrelated to this module.
